It is the number 1 thing that I dislike about SQL Server. Even something as simple as `SELECT * FROM table GROUP BY field1` will fail because you aren't grouping by the rest of the table's fields (e.g. the id field).

What I've done as a temporary (but very messy and hacky) work-around is:

``` php
    public function beforeFind(Event $event, Query $query) {
        if (!array_key_exists('count', $query->clause('select'))) {
            $query->order([$this->alias() . '.name' => 'ASC']);
        }
    }
```

which is essentially what your idea is. Also not happy with that as a solution.

